<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mukhalingam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kalinganagara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mukhalingam is a village in Srikakulam district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, identified with Kalinganagara, the early capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-ganga-dynasty">Eastern Ganga dynasty</a>. Its temples to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>, notably the Madhukeswara temple, are among the finest early examples of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a> style of architecture, dating from about the 9th to 11th centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mukhalingam.jpg" alt="Mukhalingam" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: G.N. Subrahmanyam · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:700_CE_Mukhalingeswara_Temples_Group,_Kalinga_architecture,_Mukhalingam,_Andhra_Pradesh_-_65.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
